# tooling/regression/torch_regression.env — harness infrastructure config for the MBIRTORCH
# nightly regression.  Sibling of regression.env (the jax nightly's config); the two files share
# no variable, so a torch edit can never perturb the running jax nightly.
#
# CANONICAL HOME: this harness LIVES IN and RUNS FROM the mbirjax_metrics repo — edit it here.
# Each nightly run updates a persistent metrics clone and re-execs from it (see WORK_DIR), so
# remote harness/config/state changes are always picked up and no per-node path is baked in.
#
# The user-facing run knobs (tracked branches, torch index, walltime) live in
# action_scripts/torch_run_configs.env, sourced just below.  Everything in THIS file is
# infrastructure (URLs, paths, credentials, schedule).  Sourced as bash.

source "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/../../action_scripts/torch_run_configs.env"

ENABLED=1                       # master kill-switch for the TORCH nightly only (0 = installed but
                                # the wrapper exits immediately; prefer enable/disable_torch_nightly)

# FIRE-ON-CHANGE: the wrapper wakes on POLL_SCHEDULE, reads each TORCH_TRACKED_BRANCHES tip via
# `git ls-remote`, and measures a branch ONLY when it differs from the last-measured commit
# (metrics state/<plat>/, where <plat> is gpu-torch or cpu-torch — disjoint from the jax state).
# 03:00 — one hour after the jax nightly.  Slurm allocates the two jobs separately in any case,
# so the stagger is insurance against queueing contention on the ai partition, not a correctness
# requirement (nightly_plan.md §3(a)).
POLL_SCHEDULE="0 3 * * *"

# (macOS runs at TORCH_MACOS_NIGHTLY_TIME from torch_run_configs.env; POLL_SCHEDULE is cluster-only.)

# ── Repos (URLs, not paths — the harness clones both itself) ──────────────────────────────────
METRICS_URL="https://github.com/gbuzzard/mbirjax_metrics.git"   # harness + results + state
MBIRTORCH_URL="https://github.com/cabouman/mbirtorch.git"       # library under test

# Node-independent scratch for the persistent metrics clone + throwaway library clones.  MUST be a
# different directory from the jax nightly's WORK_DIR: the wrapper uses $WORK_DIR/.lock.d as its
# single-instance lock and $WORK_DIR/metrics as the clone it pushes from, so sharing either would
# couple the two jobs (nightly_plan.md §3(a)).
#   export MBIRTORCH_REGRESSION_WORK="$SCRATCH/mbirtorch_regression"   (honored below)
WORK_DIR="${MBIRTORCH_REGRESSION_WORK:-$HOME/.mbirtorch/regression}"

# ── Build / test ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DEDICATED env — never TORCHPY or a dev env (the per-branch editable installs churn the env and
# then delete the clone they point at; a dev env inherits every campaign mutation as an
# unattributed change to the nightly's measurements — nightly_plan.md §3(f)).  Auto-created by
# lib_torch_env.sh if missing.  REG_TORCH_VENV overrides with an existing venv for TRIAL runs
# only (the pre-schedule trial uses a venv layered over TORCHPY; see lib_torch_env.sh).
CONDA_ENV="mbirtorch_regression"
# The HARNESS's own python deps (NOT mbirtorch's) — scaling_common imports these at module level.
HARNESS_DEPS="matplotlib ruamel.yaml"
RUN_TESTS=1                     # 1 = run the mbirtorch suite -> tests_<plat>_<date>.txt beside the run
                                # (the suite carries test_vs_goldens.py, the torch-vs-jax value check —
                                # the reason the nightly itself has no cross-framework column)

# ── Node preamble (cluster module loads + proxy) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Same file the jax nightly sources (module load conda + cuda + the squid proxy exports).  It is
# SOURCED in both phases and must remain source-safe: module loads + exports only, NO `exit`.
# The [ -f ] guard in the wrapper skips it on the Mac automatically.
PREAMBLE_FILE="$HOME/load_conda_cuda.sh"

# ── Transport / notify ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
MAX_PUSH_FILE_MB=25             # safety cap: the wrapper unstages any oversized result before pushing
# Unattended-push credential (cluster) — the SAME credential-store file the jax nightly uses
# (chmod 600, one line: https://<user>:<PAT>@github.com).  Both wrappers push disjoint paths with
# rebase-retry, so sharing the credential is safe.
TOKEN_FILE="$HOME/.config/mbirjax/metrics_credentials"
NOTIFY="buzzard@purdue.edu"     # slurm --mail-user for the mbirtorch-nightly job; the job name in
                                # the FAIL mail says which backend regressed before the mail is opened
